["|Case|:**add_item**\n   ```\n   CLASS InventoryManager:\n       FUNCTION __init__(self, file_path: str):\n           SET self.file_path = file_path\n           SET self.items = self.load_inventory()\n\n       FUNCTION load_inventory(self) -> list:\n           IF NOT os.path.exists(self.file_path):\n               RETURN []\n           OPEN self.file_path AS file:\n               RETURN [line.strip().split(',') FOR line IN file.readlines()]\n\n       FUNCTION save_inventory(self, items: list) -> None:\n           OPEN self.file_path AS file:\n               FOR item IN items:\n                   file.write(','.join(item) + '\\n')\n\n       FUNCTION add_item(self, name: str, category: str, quantity: int) -> None:\n           APPEND [name, category, str(quantity)] TO self.items\n           self.save_inventory(self.items)\n   ```\n|Case|:**update_item**\n   ```\n   CLASS InventoryManager:\n       FUNCTION update_item(self, name: str, quantity: int) -> None:\n           FOR item IN self.items:\n               IF item[0] == name:\n                   SET item[2] = str(quantity)\n                   BREAK\n           self.save_inventory(self.items)\n   ```\n", '|Case|:**search_item**\n   ```\n   CLASS InventoryManager:\n       FUNCTION search_item(self, query: str) -> list:\n           RETURN [item FOR item IN self.items IF query.lower() IN item[0].lower() OR query.lower() IN item[1].lower()]\n   ```\n\n#### Special Third-Party Library Usage:\n- **`tkinter`**: A standard GUI toolkit in Python which is used for creating interactive applications. It provides methods for creating windows, dialog boxes, buttons, lists, etc.\n- **`os`**: A standard library that provides functions for interacting with the operating system, like checking for file existence and manipulating file paths.']
